WEBVTT

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.700
Saga...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.860
I wasn't paying attention.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.960
I'd been trying to just watch him from afar...

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.340
Uh, I'm sorry. Please take the book.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.020
Why do you know my name?

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.930
I'd been watching him for three years at school.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.240
This is the 4th year.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.350
I'd decided to keep everything locked away in my heart.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.250
Yet, as soon as he was in front of me,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.710
all my feelings poured out of me.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:01.170
I was desperately trying to contain it, but it was in vain.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.230
I love you, I love you, I love you.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.960
I'm in love with you.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.250
I, uh, I mean...

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.190
Back then, everything was so pure.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.580
Marukawa Shoten Publishing Co.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.690
And now, ten years later...

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.860
At age 25, I, Ritsu Onodera,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.280
have become a totally jaded adult.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:55.470
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:55.470
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:01.010
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:01.010
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.640
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.640
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.440
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.440
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.440
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.440
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.280
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.280
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.660
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.660
If I reach out my hand

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.040
hajimete no kimochi

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.040
Will you understand my feelings?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.420
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.420
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.800
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.800
I love you more and more every second

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.930
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.930
We're still far from a happy ending

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:50.900
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:50.900
But I want to make it come true

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.370
tsuzuite yuku

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.370
Our story continues

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.530
I'm being assigned to the shojo manga department?!

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.620
But...please!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.720
I'm sure we discussed this during my interview.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.260
I told you that I was the literature editor...

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.140
...at my previous company,

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.500
and that I wanted to stay in that field!

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.540
Could you please look into that again?!

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.480
But it says right here:

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.900
"Mid-Career Recruitment of Ritsu Onodera...

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.980
...into the Shojo Manga department...

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.550
...at Marukawa Publishing."

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:29.040
Now, let me show you to the editorial department.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.650
Are you ready?

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.150
This sucks!

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.390
I quit my last job because I
wanted to work on literature!

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.650
So why the hell am I
stuck with manga now?!

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.580
Besides...

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.020
Isn't working on shojo manga
basically a dead-end job for a guy?

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.410
That's not true.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.040
It's true that that department...

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.630
...was kind of a dead weight until recently,

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.750
but since the new editor-in-chief joined last year,

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.270
it's been really good.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.140
They were the top in sales,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.940
and even received an award from the CEO.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:03.930
Okay...

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:09.300
And on top of that, all of the
editors are really handsome.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.340
Huh? All of the editors are male?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.640
Yes. There are actually quite a few...

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.620
...female employees who have their eyes on them.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.350
At the beginning of the cycle,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.820
it's like the air is full of dreamy pheromones or something.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.570
Cycle?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.570
You'll understand when you see it.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.880
To be honest, I want to leave right now,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.500
but I suppose I can't really do that.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:37.500
I guess I'll come here for two
weeks and find a reason to quit.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.190
Excuse me. I'm from the general affairs department.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.760
I brought the new employee who's starting today.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.670
Oh, Emerald? Over there.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:47.890
Thank you.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.510
If I'm going to quit anyway,

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:56.320
I guess I can check out that amazing editor-in-chief.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.850
It might be helpful for me at my next company.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.220
Rebuilding something like this is no small feat.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.820
I'm sure he must have really grasped the way...

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.920
...the market moved and came
up with a detailed plan.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.450
Nice to meet you. My name is Ritsu Onodera.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.460
I'll be working with you starting today.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.100
Yeah, must be a detailed and proper...

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.340
Proper...

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.570
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.470
It looks like there was a mistake with the cycle!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.030
Good luck!

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.790
Huh? Wait!

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.660
Excuse me, the Emerald editors...

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.830
Uh...

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.600
It's not us.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.480
Why are you avoiding me?

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.010
Stench

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.610
Is this what she meant with "cycle?"

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.490
("Cycle" and "stench" are homonyms.)

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.490
I guess it smells like a bunch of bikers...

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.800
Um, excuse me?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.250
Um...

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.250
What?

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.680
That's what I'd like to know!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:07.260
Sorry, I'm the new guy who's starting today.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.650
Oh, was that today?

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:14.140
Takano, the new guy's here.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.140
Takano?

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.490
Shut up!

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.320
I heard you the first time.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.780
Editor-in-chief?

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.540
This?

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.300
Proper

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.260
Proper

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.450
So what are you? A part timer?

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.210
I'm an employee; contract based though.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.850
Your name?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.580
My name is Ritsu Onodera.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.040
Oh, yeah, they said that
someone like you had come.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.220
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:44.800
Nice to meet you.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.780
I couldn't be there for the interview,

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.800
but you have worked as an editor, right?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.670
Yes, I worked at Onodera
Publishing for three years.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.760
Teen magazine? Adolescent magazine?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:58.060
Oh, no, I've always worked on literature.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.420
Literature?

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.310
Yes.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.440
This guy...

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.750
So this is your first time with manga?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.690
Yes...

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.450
Dude, don't judge people
based on their first impression.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:10.650
Useless!

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.700
This guy... is horrible.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.850
Takano, the sub mat is done.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.370
Okay. New guy, follow me.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.080
Huh?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.730
You'll have to learn to work.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.380
Sub mat means a substitute material, right?

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.470
Does that mean someone didn't deliver?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.510
Yes.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:33.890
For this month?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.800
Yes.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.980
I'm sorry, when's the release date?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.140
In seven days.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.890
In seven days? At the stores?!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.350
If the substitute material just got done,

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.150
when did they start working on it?

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.530
Three days ago.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.110
Are you serious?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:50.350
Uh, don't you have some stock sub mat?

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.680
New artist's work, etc?

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.120
We've got too much of it, but it's all useless.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:58.380
But isn't that a given with sub mat?

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.020
Whether you're an editor or an author,

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.570
if you think that "sub mat" is just a filler,

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:04.630
you're an idiot.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.380
If there's a hole, cram a diamond in there,

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.280
even if it's rough.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:10.510
That's common sense.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:16.510
That's true, but that's nothing
but the best case scenario.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.760
Good work.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.180
I'm sorry for telling you to finish it in three days.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.360
It's not a problem, I've got the time.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:27.290
Did you bring your tools?

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.360
Oh, yes.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.150
Can you make this kissing scene more dramatic?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.610
Something like this?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.970
No, more like from this angle.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:45.600
Are you going to make her redraw it now?

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.550
Aren't you making the printers wait?

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.270
No, not like that. Here.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.640
You have kissed someone before, right?

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.680
Hey, now! That's sexual harassment!

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.800
Uh, isn't it fine the way it is now?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.930
It's drawn well enough as it is, and we don't have time.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.140
I'm just saying it because I know it can be better.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.660
Stay out of it, noob.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.220
Noob?!

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:12.370
Ah, but even if you do it, you can't see yourself.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.690
That is true.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.550
All right, I'll show you an example
so please draw it real quick.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.230
Oh, references right? I'll go get some.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:25.160
From this angle so you can
see the chin, slightly titled.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:25.960
Uh...

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:37.980
Did you get that?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.600
Then please ink it real quick.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.840
Wh-What the hell are you doing?!

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:47.600
What do you mean? Work, of course.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:52.150
This jerk...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:58.400
So those two weeks...
I probably won't make it.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.690
What I learned so far:

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.830
The Emerald editorial team...

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.670
...is a collection of weirdos and
is avoided by the other teams.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:14.990
It seems they have a passion
for shojo manga. Passion?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.130
Yeah, passionate indeed.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.380
I mean they even go as far
as becoming a model for them.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.750
I would have never imagined
that I would be sexually harassed,

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.330
on my first day...

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.730
My stomach hurts.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.480
I wanted to work with literature.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:39.310
All I want to do is make books that
people will want to treasure.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.840
Since my father was the
CEO of a publishing house,

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.830
I've always liked books.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:51.000
So I joined my father's company
without any ulterior motives.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:55.070
As soon as I joined I was
managing a star writer,

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:57.130
and while I felt the
pressure, I was happy.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:03.050
But making books is a process that
takes much longer than I thought.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.790
And especially with hardcover books.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.140
Each one is like a work of art.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.640
The meetings with the author.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.690
The discussions with the designer.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.810
What kind of image to use for the front cover?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:18.650
What about the spine?
The bookmark? What color?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.810
Seeing a book that I poured
that much of your heart into...

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:24.760
...sell makes me happier than anything else.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.410
That's all I wanted...

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.360
This month's top seller was
Onodera's author again.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.880
What? Again?

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.780
Seriously, it must be so easy once
you get in through a connection.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.840
I hear that.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.930
Unlike us, he got that star author,

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.020
even though he just joined.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.010
It's so unfair. We work our asses off,

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:46.050
but still only get the low ranking authors.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.590
And the sales...

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:49.680
That's just because of the
authors and the sales team.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.650
It doesn't make sense...

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:54.360
...that he gets rated so highly
if he can't do anything...

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.860
...but hand in the manuscript.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.140
Seriously.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:06.870
It's not like I felt like I
intended to get through a connection,

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.580
and I thought that I was
working as hard as I could.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:17.330
The old me would have never
been able to recover from that shock.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.090
But at this point I was already jaded, so...

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:24.290
Screw you! Then there's no
problem if I quit this company right now,

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:27.100
and make books that sell millions at another company.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.470
...that was how I dealt with it.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.770
Even I have to admit that
my personality's twisted.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:39.110
Wait, it's not like I wanted this.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.050
I'm in love with you.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:42.990
Since then...

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.710
I've started to think...

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.110
...about things with the
worst case outcome first.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.780
By doing so, even if you did
get hurt a little bit,

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.520
it wouldn't end up being a lasting wound.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:02.620
I have to snap out of it!

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:05.710
Stop thinking about someone whose
face you can't even remember!

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.900
The task at hand is how to quit this job,

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.060
so that I gain the most out
of this for my next job!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:10.760
Hey.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.520
What?!

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.690
Did you finish submitting the manuscript?

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.400
Yeah, thanks.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:22.080
Hey, you're not even going
to apologize for that kiss?

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.470
I just confirmed this with my boss,

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:27.540
but you're the son of the
Onodera Publishing house, right?

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.680
There's no connection
between the company and me.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.170
Are you dissatisfied being here,
since you wanted to do literature?

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.170
Yes, totally!

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.730
No. How should I put this?

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:44.460
Shojo mangas have a heavy romantic focus.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.410
I'm not really very good at that sort of stuff,

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:50.750
or don't really have a good idea...

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.590
To be honest, I don't really
understand romance anyway...

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:57.060
If you're not motivated, quit
because you'll just get in the way.

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:04.570
How many people do you think
get to do the thing they love for work?

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:05.740
That...

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.760
Everybody starts as a noob.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.000
Huh?

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:14.330
Is he actually trying to cheer me up?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.830
Well, useless people are useless
no matter what they do.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.840
I'll kill you!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:26.780
Newbie, the others have gone
home, so you can go home, too.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:27.840
My name is Onodera!

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:30.290
Listen.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.250
Yes?

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:34.540
Have we met before?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.800
I don't know...

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:45.270
A true dump...

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:58.030
If I give up now, nothing will have changed.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.650
If I give my best and am
told that I'm useless,

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.260
then that's my own fault.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:07.800
But being considered useless,
without having even tried,

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.520
is something I can't allow.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:12.140
I'm going to show him.

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:13.640
Going home?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.800
To a meeting.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:15.970
Bye.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.790
Oh, man, I'm sleepy.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:41.830
I guess reading 100 shojo mangas
in one night is exhausting.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.040
And my stomach aches,

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:48.420
just thinking that I have to
spend the whole day in that dump.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.930
Good morning...

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.930
Good morning, Onodera!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.110
Oh, I'm sorry, I made
a mistake. Emerald...

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.280
What are you talking about? We're here!

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.920
Sorry about yesterday.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.440
We just barely got the manuscript in
before the deadline, so it's all good again.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.280
So this is your first
time working on manga?

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.450
Don't worry.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.540
We'll teach you the ropes!

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.250
Excuse me, I have to go to the bathroom.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.960
No, please! I'm not part
of the Emerald team!

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.960
I know, I mean sorry.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.060
My eyesight should be
good, but what is that?!

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:29.990
Huh?

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:33.100
I remember that it was a real
dump back there yesterday.

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:35.210
I can accept that it's been cleaned up,

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:38.180
but why have the corpses morphed
into a group of calm young men?!

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.850
And what is with that pink
overflow in that office?

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.200
That's the beginning of the cycle.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.360
What exactly is that?

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.460
You know about the 20 day garden radish right?

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.030
And you can harvest it in 20 days.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:53.360
Yeah?

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:57.240
Those guys make a book in 20 day cycles.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:58.810
Editor's work

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:58.810
Still normal - [Script check] - Seed

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.920
So kind of like this...

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:00.600
Still fine - [Storyboard check] - Two leaves

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.350
Not so fine - [Draft check] - Four leaves

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:04.100
Haven't gone home - [Accept manuscript] - Growing

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
Haven't bathed

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
1 Normal time frame for manuscript

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
2 Tight time frame for man.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
3 Ridiculous time frame for man.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
Growing

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.850
Deadly time frame for man.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:07.890
And then when everything is over,

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:07.610
[Galley proof] - More growth

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:08.730
[End] - Grows a lot

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.300
those guys morph.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.760
So what about that pink room?

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:16.130
You know the saying,

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.420
when in Rome, do as the Romans do, right?

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.310
In order to understand how the readers feel,

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.140
Takano said that they have to approach it...

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.890
...by duplicating the environment.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:28.120
W-Well, since they're actually successful,

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.860
I don't think it'll be a bad place to be.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.400
Even though they have created
quite a few legends...

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.280
Legends? Like what?

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:38.170
Please don't make me say that!

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:39.780
Anyway, good luck!

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:45.910
Oh, yeah, those people are
called the maiden club.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.670
Maiden club...

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.080
Hi!

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.420
Hiya.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.930
This is a photocomposition sheet.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.900
Lately most of the manuscripts are digital,

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.190
so we don't need to use these that much,

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.260
but it's a basic skill you should have.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:14.020
Oh, watch out so you don't go crooked.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:14.950
Okay.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.160
They say "A crooked photocomposition
is a sign of a crooked heart."

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.450
Kisa, you were crooked last time.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.090
What? Really? Where?

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:23.970
This month, page 12...

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:23.610
What's the matter?

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.070
I was just wondering if this
author ran out of time.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:28.710
Why?

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:36.200
But still I...

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:32.310
The two page spread is mostly white.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.830
And this panel just has toner and text.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.220
It seems half-assed.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:37.720
You fool!

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.720
What was that for?!

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.480
You idiot!

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.220
That's a maiden's heart throb panel!

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:44.850
Throb?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.730
Yes, look at it!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.640
This is the scene where the main character...

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.530
...and her male partner finally
get over being stubborn...

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.480
...and admit their love for each other.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.410
In the first person view,

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:58.490
the reader gets easily emotionally involved.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.520
That's why it's important...

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:04.240
to slowly ramp up her expectation
that "something's coming."

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.440
For instance, as the
emotions get more intense,

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.210
you make the photocomposition bigger.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.780
And when you have reached the peak...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.980
I love you...

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.120
...you drop the bomb.

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:19.170
Aw, you understand
this feeling, right?

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.630
Not at all.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:24.010
Well, I kind of get what
you're trying to say.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.820
But what I don't get with such scenes,

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:28.940
is why everything gets so
white and randomly sparkly.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.140
And the abundant use of toner,

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.650
and why the hair and clothing flow
even though there's no wind.

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.820
And even though it's a manga,

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.340
should the main character be allowed
to reach happiness so quickly?

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.530
Well, I guess it happens
because it is manga, but...

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:46.720
Maybe the reason I believe reality is crueler...

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.930
...is because I've never really loved?

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:53.020
There was a time when I believed that...

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.710
..."Hard work will pay off" or "Your
feelings will always reach them."

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:59.830
I don't know if it's a blessing or a curse...

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.840
...that I found out that that's a myth.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:08.320
What should I do...

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:05.330
If that's what it means to become an adult,

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.310
it's not necessarily unfortunate,
but really mundane.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:16.470
But it's not like I'm being negative,

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:19.100
I just turned my back
and am moving forward...

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:25.870
I can't shake the feeling
that I've met you before,

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:27.530
but I can't remember where.

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:30.130
Don't touch me.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.360
Well, since we lived in the same area,

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:32.630
we might have passed each other.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:35.500
And as we're working
in the same business,

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.340
we might have been at the printers
at the same time or something.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.500
Ah, I guess that's true.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.670
Hey, Rittie?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.950
What are you doing with
that manga catalog?

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.300
Rittie?

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.170
Since I just started with manga,

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:54.330
I thought I'd memorize
our catalog of manga.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.740
Seriously?

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:58.820
Do you know how many
thousands of books we have?

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.640
Oh, I'm not just memorizing the titles,

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.320
I'm actually reading the books, so...

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.240
Impossible, I could never do that!

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.040
Oh, I used to do stuff like...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.320
...read all the library books
at my school regularly, so...

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.500
Is something wrong?

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.260
Not really.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.110
What the hell?

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:28.920
I bet you think that memorizing
our works is normal.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.640
See you. Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:43.900
I won't let Takano think that I'm useless!

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:58.840
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:58.840
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:04.220
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:04.220
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:12.310
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:12.310
I fell in love with you

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:15.800
yuugure no kaze no nioi

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:15.800
In a sunset, filled with the scent of the wind

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:20.730
boku wa omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:20.730
When I remember your voice and your smile

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:25.650
kimi no koe sono waraikata

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:25.650
I'm instantly happy

00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:29.950
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:29.950
I fell in love with you

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.870
dare ni mo mada ietenai

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.870
But I haven't been able to tell anyone yet

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:38.330
hitori omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:38.330
When I remember your voice and the way you talk

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:42.840
sono koe shaberi kata

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:42.840
Even though I'm alone I'll be happy

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:48.000
samishii kimochi potsuri

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:48.000
The feeling of loneliness... isolated

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.430
sukina kimochi kirari

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.430
The feeling of love... sparkling

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:56.940
futatsu kubetsu ga tsukanai boku wa

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:56.940
I'm unable to tell these two feelings apart

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:01.550
yuugure ni kokoro tsuburete ku

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:01.550
My heart is slowly crushed as the sun sets

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.940
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.940
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:10.410
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:10.410
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:14.790
asa no hikari ga afure dashitara

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:14.790
Once the morning light pours in

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:20.880
suki to yuou yuuki motte

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:20.880
I'll courageously say I love you

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:27.190
Jargon used in Marukawa Shoten Publishing Co.!

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:29.650
I'd like to talk about some of the jargon we use around here.

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:31.130
Jargon #1: Dead Submission Date.

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:34.420
Dead Submission Date refers to the deadline
for when we are to submit manuscripts.

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:36.380
Anything submitted past this
deadline makes publishers angry.

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:39.890
As a result, if we pass the Dead Submission Date,
magazines and books cannot be published on time.
